# PandamStyle: regenerable run output.
# The committed part of a run (env.json, summary.json, REPORT.md, per-step logs,
# artifact-digests.txt) stays tracked; the heavy artifacts and the pilot work
# tree do not. The pattern is per-directory so every run directory is treated
# the same way, including the ones that do not exist yet.
out-pandamstyle/
evidence/*/artifacts/
evidence/*/pilot/
# A verification run directory can be nested one level deeper than the patterns
# above (evidence/performance/<batch>/verify/...), and the same rule applies to
# it: the committed part of a run is env.json, summary.json, steps.tsv and the
# per-step logs; the pilot work tree and the generated artifacts are not.
evidence/**/artifacts/
evidence/**/pilot/
# Raw step logs are evidence and stay tracked, like the historical ones.
!evidence/*/*.log
examples/pilots/vite-react/.pandamstyle/
examples/pilots/vite-react/dist/
examples/pilots/vite-react/node_modules/
packages/compiler/__tests__/pandamstyle/fixtures/*/generated/

# PandamStyle benchmark scratch: generated corpora, per-job project copies and
# the raw observation stream. Everything here is REGENERABLE from the committed
# corpus manifests and the harness, and the corpora are benchmark INPUT whose
# byte content is the identity of every number taken against it. The committed
# evidence lives in evidence/performance/spike-1/.
.pms-bench/
.pms-test-support/
